{title: Your Love Makes Me Sing (FJ_82_en)}
{subtitle: Du begeisterst mich / Hallelujah}
{song_number: 82}
{language: en}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 98}
{comment: Verse 1}
[C]Your love is amazing, [G]steady and unchanging.
[C]Your love is a mountain, [Dsus4]firm beneath my feet.
[C]Your love is a mystery, [G]how You gently lift me
[C]when I am surrounded; [Dsus4]Your love carries me.

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]Your love is surprising, [G]I can feel it rising,
[C]all the joy that's growing [Dsus4]deep inside of me.
[C]Ev'ry time I see You, [G]all Your goodness shines through;
[C]I can feel this God song [Dsus4]rising up in me.

{comment: Chorus}
[G]Hallelujah, Hallelu[Dsus4]jah, Hallelu[Em7]jah,
[C]Your love makes me sing. [G]Hallelujah, Hallelu[Dsus4]jah,
[Em7]Hallelujah, [C]Your love makes me sing.
{comment: Repeat chorus after verse 2; repeat “Your love makes me sing” at the end.}
{comment: Brian Doerksen and Brenton Brown. Source: pp. 146–147.}
